-- title:
--   Order and cyclicity of H² of idèle classes, p-group case
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $F$ be number fields with $F$ an $E$-algebra and $F/E$ Galois, let $p$ be a prime, and assume the Galois group $F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} F$ is a $p$-group in the sense of `IsPGroup`. Let $D$ be an idèle Galois descent datum for $\mathcal O_F \subseteq F$ over $E$: a monoid homomorphism $g \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ from the Galois group to the ring automorphisms of the adèle ring `AdeleRing (𝓞 F) F`, each $D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ continuous and satisfying $D.\mathrm{act}\,g\,(\iota x) = \iota(g x)$ for $x \in F$, where $\iota$ is the structure map $F \to$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 F) F`. Suppose the Galois group acts multiplicatively and distributively on the idèle class group `IdeleClassGroup (𝓞 F) F`, the quotient of the units of the adèle ring by the subgroup of principal idèles (the image of $F^\times$ under $\iota$), and that this action agrees pointwise with $D.\mathrm{classAct}$, the automorphism of the quotient induced by the unit automorphism attached to $D.\mathrm{act}\,g$. Then, for the representation of the Galois group on the idèle class group arising from this action, there is a class $u \in H^2$ such that $H^2$ has cardinality equal to the cardinality of the Galois group and the $\mathbb Z$-span of $\{u\}$ is everything; that is, $H^2$ is cyclic of order exactly $[F:E]$, generated by $u$.
--
--   This is the existence of the global fundamental class together with the exact computation $\#H^2(G,C_F) = |G|$, one half of the assertion that the idèle classes of a number field form a class formation, here for Galois $p$-group layers and at the full group only. It feeds the three-part version for all subgroups, [`M4aHerbrand.exists_fundamentalClass_ideleClassGroup_of_isPGroup`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_fundamentalClass_ideleClassGroup_of_isPGroup), and the subsequent comparison of the global class with the local fundamental classes.
